# Capacitor. android/ is deliberately TRACKED, not ignored: the APK is built
# from it (docs/mobile_release.md), so the manifest, gradle config and
# resources are release inputs, not regenerable scaffold. Listing it here
# only ever misled the next person -- .gitignore does not untrack files that
# are already in the index, so the entries were inert and wrong.
# Regenerating a fresh platform instead: npx cap add android, then copy the
# release-relevant values (applicationId, RECORD_AUDIO, backup rules).
ios/
